{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of the theorem of Jensen Kohlmeyer and Liam Kruer (2026) resolving the radius-2 question in Ben Green's Open Problem 40: the asymptotic binary linear covering density f(2) equals 1. Using admissible binary quadratic maps and a codimension-doubling interpolation step, we construct linear covering subspaces of radius 2 of arbitrarily large ambient dimension whose covering density approaches 1, matching `Green40.green_40.f_two_eq_one` verbatim from google-deepmind/formal-conjectures.",
